<!-- The W.D.N.Y. memorandum of law's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of
     the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; no W.D.N.Y. rule names a face) at 12 pt (size 24 half points, Local
     Rule 10(a)(1)); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double, Local Rule 10(a)(2) double spaced) with a
     half-inch first-line indent; the court title, caption, cover title, counsel, heading, quotation and signature
     lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single); letter page with 1-inch margins on all sides (Local Rule 10(a)(4)).
     docx/nywd-motion-brief.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing and the sections: the cover unnumbered, the table
     of contents in lower roman from i, the body from 1, each page number centered at the bottom, its line 36 pt above
     the page foot (720 twips: where typst sets it, footer-descent 30 %). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="24" body="480" single="276" indent="720" heading="276" heading-before="276" heading-after="276" footer="720"/>
